    {
      "title": "More part-time bosses and co-CEOs could keep women in leadership and narrow Australia’s pay gap",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/more-part-time-bosses-and-co-ceos-could-keep-women-in-leadership-and-narrow-australias-pay-gap",
      "description": "<p>Uneven caring responsibilities combined with a lack of flexible work options have prevented women from staying in senior positions, research suggests</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/13/labor-anthony-albanese-charity-boost-greens-ukraine-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia politics live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>More part-time bosses and “co-CEOs” could keep women in leadership and narrow Australia’s gender pay gap, the federal government’s Workplace Gender Equality Agency says.</p><p>WGEA warned resistance to gender equality was growing and urged employers to make management more flexible to reduce the gender pay gap, where women earn $0.79 for every $1 a man makes on average.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/more-part-time-bosses-and-co-ceos-could-keep-women-in-leadership-and-narrow-australias-pay-gap\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-12T14:01:56"
    },
    {
      "title": "Rescued turtles return home after NSW government cut flows to wetland",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/rescued-turtles-return-home-after-nsw-government-cut-flows-to-wetland",
      "description": "<p>Environmental water to the area was halted after a complaint from a private landholder, leading to the deaths of wildlife and sheep</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/13/labor-anthony-albanese-charity-boost-greens-ukraine-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia politics live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Freshwater turtles rescued from a dried-up water hole in western New South Wales after the state government cut environmental water to the area are being returned home.</p><p>Late last month,<strong> </strong>10 broad-shelled turtles and three Murray River turtles were released back into the Gingham water hole in the state’s Gwydir region.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/rescued-turtles-return-home-after-nsw-government-cut-flows-to-wetland\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-12T14:00:58"
    },
    {
      "title": "Australia may risk a diplomatic spat with the Trump administration if it limits the livestream of a US execution",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/australia-us-execution-livestream-julie-inman-grant-esafety",
      "description": "<p>A history of tech giant legal challenges and US political criticism shows there’s no easy solution for the eSafety commissioner</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s online safety regulator has a few levers to limit the public seeing the US’s planned live stream of an execution but history suggests it will lead to a very public fight.</p><p>The US defense secretary, Pete Hegseth, announced last week the planned execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan would be livestreamed <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/08/hegseth-fort-hood-shooter-public-execution\">when the military execution is carried out in early December</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/australia-us-execution-livestream-julie-inman-grant-esafety\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-12T14:00:57"
    },
